1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,760
April sixteenth.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,440
Since the day the stall opened, Priya from

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,240
Infotech has taken chai for the whole floor,

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,280
every day.

5
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:10,700
On a tab.

6
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:12,280
Pay later.

7
00:00:12,831 --> 00:00:15,551
Today, Meera sends the first bill — two

8
00:00:15,631 --> 00:00:16,711
weeks of chai.

9
00:00:16,991 --> 00:00:18,511
Six thousand rupees.

10
00:00:18,751 --> 00:00:20,111
Her profit goes up.

11
00:00:20,431 --> 00:00:22,031
Her galla doesn't move.

12
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,080
So did Meera make money, or not?

13
00:00:32,307 --> 00:00:34,467
First, last time's answers.

14
00:00:34,787 --> 00:00:35,307
One.

15
00:00:35,587 --> 00:00:37,147
Is the cart an expense?

16
00:00:37,427 --> 00:00:37,827
No.

17
00:00:37,987 --> 00:00:40,747
It's still making chai, so it's an asset.

18
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:42,007
Two.

19
00:00:42,247 --> 00:00:45,127
Meera's profit: eighteen thousand of revenue,

20
00:00:45,207 --> 00:00:47,207
minus five thousand of rent.

21
00:00:47,247 --> 00:00:48,887
Thirteen thousand rupees.

22
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:50,287
Three.

23
00:00:50,487 --> 00:00:52,687
Profit lives on the right side of the scale,

24
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:54,047
inside equity.

25
00:00:54,127 --> 00:00:55,407
It belongs to Meera.

26
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:59,353
Today, Khata pins two needles on the stall's

27
00:00:59,513 --> 00:00:59,913
wall.

28
00:01:00,153 --> 00:01:01,593
The first is Profit.

29
00:01:01,993 --> 00:01:04,553
It moves when Meera earns money, or uses

30
00:01:04,593 --> 00:01:05,353
it up.

31
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:08,373
The second is Money — everything in the

32
00:01:08,413 --> 00:01:10,733
galla, plus everything in the bank.

33
00:01:11,187 --> 00:01:14,147
Right now, profit reads thirteen thousand.

34
00:01:14,227 --> 00:01:16,547
Money reads fifty-one thousand.

35
00:01:16,627 --> 00:01:19,027
It's bigger, because it also holds Meera's

36
00:01:19,107 --> 00:01:20,867
savings and Ravi Mama's loan.

37
00:01:21,427 --> 00:01:23,187
Most people think these two needles move

38
00:01:23,267 --> 00:01:23,987
together.

39
00:01:24,227 --> 00:01:25,027
Let's watch.

40
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,840
First, rewind one day.

41
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,680
April fifteenth.

42
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,920
Meera carries fifteen thousand rupees from

43
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,320
the galla to the bank.

44
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,320
Profit?

45
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:35,160
No change.

46
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:35,760
Money?

47
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,280
Also no change.

48
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:40,100
But in the books, these are two different

49
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:40,860
accounts.

50
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:42,980
Cash is the notes in the galla.

51
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:45,460
Bank is money the bank keeps for her, and

52
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,300
gives back whenever she asks.

53
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,880
Cash went down fifteen thousand.

54
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,360
Bank went up fifteen thousand.

55
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,360
So the money needle doesn't move.

56
00:01:56,408 --> 00:01:58,448
Now, April sixteenth.

57
00:01:58,648 --> 00:01:59,768
Infotech's tab.

58
00:02:00,008 --> 00:02:01,688
Which two things changed?

59
00:02:03,658 --> 00:02:06,058
Sales went up by six thousand.

60
00:02:06,098 --> 00:02:08,378
The chai has been drunk, so Meera has earned

61
00:02:08,458 --> 00:02:09,018
it.

62
00:02:09,698 --> 00:02:12,098
But on the left, no money came in.

63
00:02:12,378 --> 00:02:14,978
Instead, Infotech now owes the stall six

64
00:02:15,058 --> 00:02:16,098
thousand rupees.

65
00:02:16,338 --> 00:02:18,978
Money that customers owe you is an asset,

66
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:20,418
called a receivable.

67
00:02:20,876 --> 00:02:23,356
So the profit needle jumps, from thirteen

68
00:02:23,516 --> 00:02:25,676
thousand to nineteen thousand.

69
00:02:25,756 --> 00:02:26,756
And the money needle?

70
00:02:27,036 --> 00:02:28,556
It doesn't move at all.

71
00:02:30,164 --> 00:02:32,564
Revenue counts when it's earned — when the

72
00:02:32,724 --> 00:02:35,684
chai is drunk — not when the money arrives.

73
00:02:36,324 --> 00:02:38,444
And expenses count when they're incurred

74
00:02:38,764 --> 00:02:40,924
— when the thing is used up — not when they're

75
00:02:41,084 --> 00:02:41,724
paid.

76
00:02:42,504 --> 00:02:44,584
This idea is called accrual.

77
00:02:46,548 --> 00:02:48,068
April twentieth.

78
00:02:48,148 --> 00:02:50,548
Meera pays Gopal five thousand rupees of

79
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:53,028
the eight thousand she owes him for milk.

80
00:02:53,108 --> 00:02:54,868
Meera's sure about this one.

81
00:02:54,948 --> 00:02:57,588
Money left the galla, so it's an expense.

82
00:02:58,205 --> 00:02:58,765
Nope.

83
00:02:59,005 --> 00:03:01,565
That milk came in as stock, and Gopal became

84
00:03:01,605 --> 00:03:02,765
a liability.

85
00:03:02,925 --> 00:03:05,725
Today, Meera is only paying down that debt.

86
00:03:05,805 --> 00:03:07,165
So which needle moves?

87
00:03:09,136 --> 00:03:10,656
Only the money needle.

88
00:03:10,896 --> 00:03:12,336
Down five thousand.

89
00:03:12,536 --> 00:03:14,736
Profit stays at nineteen thousand.

90
00:03:15,276 --> 00:03:17,556
The payment shrinks a liability.

91
00:03:18,276 --> 00:03:20,636
Money the stall owes a supplier is a payable

92
00:03:21,036 --> 00:03:22,876
— the mirror of a receivable.

93
00:03:24,127 --> 00:03:25,727
April twenty-second.

94
00:03:25,807 --> 00:03:27,647
A customer pays four thousand rupees in

95
00:03:27,727 --> 00:03:30,687
advance, for a catering order on May fifth.

96
00:03:31,227 --> 00:03:32,547
Meera's quick this time.

97
00:03:32,787 --> 00:03:33,987
Money in from a customer?

98
00:03:34,387 --> 00:03:36,947
Revenue — straight into the profit pocket.

99
00:03:37,864 --> 00:03:38,384
Nope.

100
00:03:38,584 --> 00:03:40,704
Meera hasn't made a single cup yet.

101
00:03:40,904 --> 00:03:43,064
Until May fifth, she owes that customer

102
00:03:43,144 --> 00:03:45,464
an event — or their money back.

103
00:03:46,004 --> 00:03:48,604
An advance is a liability, not revenue.

104
00:03:48,924 --> 00:03:49,804
Not yet.

105
00:03:50,644 --> 00:03:52,404
Meera, which needle moves?

106
00:03:54,362 --> 00:03:56,042
Only the money needle.

107
00:03:56,162 --> 00:03:57,562
Up four thousand.

108
00:03:57,762 --> 00:03:59,882
Profit stays at nineteen thousand.

109
00:04:01,148 --> 00:04:02,988
Now you, on your own.

110
00:04:03,308 --> 00:04:04,828
April twenty-fifth.

111
00:04:04,948 --> 00:04:06,988
Infotech pays four thousand rupees of its

112
00:04:07,068 --> 00:04:08,948
tab, by UPI.

113
00:04:09,228 --> 00:04:09,948
Profit?

114
00:04:10,188 --> 00:04:10,828
Money?

115
00:04:13,987 --> 00:04:16,547
Money goes up by four thousand — straight

116
00:04:16,627 --> 00:04:17,347
into the bank.

117
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:19,227
The galla never even sees it.

118
00:04:19,827 --> 00:04:21,187
Profit doesn't move.

119
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:24,267
Meera earned that money back on April sixteenth.

120
00:04:24,467 --> 00:04:26,347
Today, she's only collecting it.

121
00:04:27,047 --> 00:04:30,007
The receivable shrinks, and the bank grows.

122
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:33,580
Since April fifteenth, the profit needle

123
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:36,740
moved once — on the day no money came in.

124
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:39,940
The money needle moved three times — and

125
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,860
not one of those was profit.

126
00:04:42,412 --> 00:04:44,972
Profit: nineteen thousand rupees.

127
00:04:45,212 --> 00:04:47,532
Money: fifty-four thousand.

128
00:04:48,212 --> 00:04:49,332
Two needles.

129
00:04:49,412 --> 00:04:50,772
Two different stories.

130
00:04:51,518 --> 00:04:54,798
Cash basis counts money only when it moves.

131
00:04:55,418 --> 00:04:58,018
Accrual basis counts revenue when it's earned,

132
00:04:58,058 --> 00:05:00,258
and expenses when they're incurred.

133
00:05:01,038 --> 00:05:03,198
Businesses use accrual, because it shows

134
00:05:03,278 --> 00:05:05,358
what was really earned — even while the

135
00:05:05,438 --> 00:05:06,958
money is still on its way.

136
00:05:08,229 --> 00:05:09,909
So — two needles.

137
00:05:10,149 --> 00:05:12,629
Earned isn't the same as received.

138
00:05:12,869 --> 00:05:15,189
Paid isn't the same as used up.

139
00:05:15,589 --> 00:05:17,669
Profit is not cash.

140
00:05:18,813 --> 00:05:19,493
Your turn.

141
00:05:19,693 --> 00:05:20,693
Three quick ones.

142
00:05:20,893 --> 00:05:21,373
One.

143
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:23,533
The four-thousand-rupee catering advance

144
00:05:23,853 --> 00:05:25,213
— is it revenue in April?

145
00:05:25,693 --> 00:05:26,133
Two.

146
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:28,733
Paying Gopal — is that an expense?

147
00:05:28,973 --> 00:05:29,533
Three.

148
00:05:29,773 --> 00:05:32,493
After the UPI payment, how much does Infotech

149
00:05:32,573 --> 00:05:33,613
still owe Meera?

150
00:05:33,853 --> 00:05:36,013
Answers at the start of the next lesson.

151
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,354
And now — Checkpoint two.

152
00:05:39,594 --> 00:05:41,434
Back to Aman's samosa cart.

153
00:05:41,554 --> 00:05:42,714
Five things happen.

154
00:05:42,794 --> 00:05:44,874
For each one, write down what it does to

155
00:05:45,114 --> 00:05:46,874
profit, and to cash.

156
00:05:47,335 --> 00:05:47,935
One.

157
00:05:48,135 --> 00:05:50,695
Cash sales of nine thousand rupees.

158
00:05:50,855 --> 00:05:51,335
Two.

159
00:05:51,415 --> 00:05:54,135
He pays two thousand rupees of stall rent.

160
00:05:54,295 --> 00:05:54,775
Three.

161
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,935
He supplies a school canteen with fifteen

162
00:05:57,015 --> 00:05:59,655
hundred rupees of samosas, on credit.

163
00:05:59,735 --> 00:06:00,375
Four.

164
00:06:00,455 --> 00:06:03,255
He pays Sharma Kirana two thousand rupees.

165
00:06:03,495 --> 00:06:04,055
Five.

166
00:06:04,135 --> 00:06:06,455
A customer gives him a thousand-rupee advance,

167
00:06:06,495 --> 00:06:08,375
for a birthday party next month.

168
00:06:08,495 --> 00:06:10,935
Pause the video now, and try all five.

169
00:06:14,097 --> 00:06:14,497
Ready?

170
00:06:14,977 --> 00:06:15,457
One.

171
00:06:15,697 --> 00:06:17,537
Nine thousand of cash sales.

172
00:06:17,697 --> 00:06:20,737
Profit and cash both go up nine thousand.

173
00:06:20,817 --> 00:06:21,457
Two.

174
00:06:21,497 --> 00:06:23,297
Two thousand of stall rent.

175
00:06:23,417 --> 00:06:25,377
Both go down two thousand.

176
00:06:25,537 --> 00:06:26,017
Three.

177
00:06:26,057 --> 00:06:27,937
Fifteen hundred of samosas to the school

178
00:06:28,017 --> 00:06:29,297
canteen, on credit.

179
00:06:29,697 --> 00:06:31,457
Profit up fifteen hundred.

180
00:06:31,657 --> 00:06:32,977
Cash, nothing.

181
00:06:33,057 --> 00:06:33,377
Four.

182
00:06:33,697 --> 00:06:35,857
Paying Sharma Kirana two thousand.

183
00:06:36,017 --> 00:06:37,537
Cash down two thousand.

184
00:06:37,737 --> 00:06:40,417
Profit, nothing — it's a debt being paid.

185
00:06:40,897 --> 00:06:41,617
Five.

186
00:06:41,657 --> 00:06:43,577
The thousand-rupee birthday advance.

187
00:06:43,777 --> 00:06:45,457
Cash up one thousand.

188
00:06:45,657 --> 00:06:47,777
Profit, nothing — it isn't earned yet.

189
00:06:48,777 --> 00:06:51,337
Aman's profit so far: eight thousand five

190
00:06:51,417 --> 00:06:52,377
hundred rupees.

191
00:06:53,888 --> 00:06:56,568
Next time — remember that bank deposit?

192
00:06:56,848 --> 00:06:58,448
Meera's phone buzzed.

193
00:06:58,528 --> 00:07:00,928
Your account is credited with fifteen thousand

194
00:07:01,008 --> 00:07:01,808
rupees.

195
00:07:01,848 --> 00:07:02,928
Credited!

196
00:07:03,088 --> 00:07:04,608
Great news… right?
